* feat: add Claude Code minimum version check to gt doctor (gt-9me)

Gas Town depends on Claude Code features added between v1.0.38 and v2.1.3.
The highest watermark is Skills (v2.0.20), used by crew-commit, ghi-list,
pr-list, and pr-sheriff. This adds:

- internal/deps/claude.go: version detection and comparison (min v2.0.20,
  recommended v2.1.3+)
- internal/doctor/claude_binary_check.go: gt doctor check that warns when
  Claude Code is missing or below minimum
- docs/design/claude-code-minimum-version.md: full research with feature
  dependency chain, version timeline, and fragile-dependency inventory
- docs/INSTALLING.md: updated Claude Code version from "latest" to ">= 2.0.20"

Claude Code is optional (not-found = OK), so the check warns rather than
errors when the version is too old.

* Remove design doc from PR scope

The research doc is useful internally but not needed in the
contribution — the code and INSTALLING.md change stand on their own.

